tatistic":"mean(b) - mean(a)","stream":"fixture_measure/measure/regret_bootstrap","warnings":[]},"fixture_notice":"FIXTURE CHECK - mechanics only, not evidence about the robot, the simulator, TabPFN or any trained student","format":"learned-judgment/snn-student-measurement/v1","label":"Measurements of one dream-trained spiking student from runs of its deployed numpy network. Decision quality is measured inside held-out dreams (dreamed objective scores), not on the robot or in the simulator; energy figures are estimates; latency is wall-clock time on this machine.","latency":{"blas":[{"architecture":"Haswell","internal_api":"openblas","num_threads":22,"prefix":"libscipy_openblas","threading_layer":"pthreads","user_api":"blas","version":"0.3.34.237.2"},{"architecture":"Haswell","internal_api":"openblas","num_threads":22,"prefix":"libscipy_openblas","threading_layer":"pthreads","user_api":"blas","version":"0.3.31.dev"}],"cpu_count":22,"decision_path":"SNNStudent.decide_index on one situation reshaped to (1, S): finite check -> InputEncoder.encode -> SpikingNetwork.decide (numpy) -> candidate index; the action lookup spec.candidate_actions is not timed","label":"wall-clock latency of the deployed numpy decision path on this machine (a measurement)","layer_sizes":[4,64,35],"median_s":0.0002299,"n_decisions":1000,"n_inputs":1000,"network_sha256":"988282fa252fd7dd2729a82380a49c9c4ad5873872b925a8d8bc68420287e281","numpy_version":"2.5.5","p95_s":0.00038082999999999997,"platform":"Windows-11-10.0.26300-SP0","processor":"Intel64 Family 6 Model 170 Stepping 4, GenuineIntel","protocol":"learned_judgment.eval.harness.measure_latency: call i decides situation i mod n; each call is timed alone with time.perf_counter_ns; no warm-up calls; median and p95 (numpy 'linear' quantile) over all calls","python_version":"3.13.16","single_row_vs_batch_decisions_differing":0,"situations":{"n":1000,"sha256":"e0b0b7227ce6ca301dc8d00a8df39ba708832aa6f9c28a650998e9fed827a2de"},"time_steps":10,"timer":"time.perf_counter_ns","torch_free_process":false,"torch_in_sys_modules_after":true,"torch_in_sys_modules_before":true},"operations":{"break_even":{"definition":"under the main estimate a hidden layer's spikes cost e_ac per synapse per spike and the dense reference costs e_mac per synapse once per decision, so the spiking connection costs less than the dense one when the layer's firing rate per step is below e_mac / (e_ac * T)","formula":"e_mac / (e_ac * T)","per_layer":[{"below_break_even":true,"firing_rate_per_step":0.2168796875,"layer":0}],"rate_per_step":0.5111111111111111},"caveats":["Energy figures are analytical estimates from operation counts and published 45 nm CMOS per-operation energies. They are not measurements. The networks ran on a CPU laptop with dense matrix arithmetic, where a spiking network does not save energy.","The estimate counts arithmetic only. Memory accesses for weights and membrane state, data movement, addressing, static power and spike communication are excluded, although published analyses find that memory accesses dominate.","The result depends on conventions: arithmetic precision, whether the real-valued first layer is counted once or at every time step, and whether neuron leak, bias and reset updates are counted. The variant including neuron updates is reported next to the main estimate.","The dense reference is a non-spiking network with the same layer sizes whose operation count follows from its architecture. No such network was trained, so the comparison says nothing about whether it would reach the same decision quality.","Teacher (TabPFN) inference energy is not included. The comparison is per student decision."],"dense_reference_macs":2496,"energy_estimate":{"caveats":["Energy figures are analytical estimates from operation counts and published 45 nm CMOS per-operation energies. They are not measurements. The networks ran on a CPU laptop with dense matrix arithmetic, where a spiking network does not save energy.","The est